  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SHOREBIRD CONSERVATION IN BRAZIL &amp; DELAWARE BAY</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project will address key conservation knowledge gaps and empower proactive conservation planning and action by delineating critical wintering habitats for 8 shorebird species, mapping areas most threatened by shrimp farming, and translating all products into Portuguese to introduce the work to key Brazilian biologists and conservation policy specialists. The companion match-funded project restored 1.4 miles of Delaware Bay beach stopover habitat for the same populations of shorebirds wintering in Brazil. Benefitted species include willet, whimbrel, ruddy turnstone, red knot, sanderling and short-billed dowitcher.</narrative>
  </description>
